  "result": "I revised the node record and wrote it to `record.jsonl`, but nothing has been run against it, so it is untested against the gate.\n\n**The gate failure (unanchored intersection, spans k10/k11):** the intersection the left-turn intention points at is now tied to the subject through the road it is on.\n- The record claims `st.intersection`, `st.on_way`, `st.highway` and `rel.occupies` for k11.\n- Exception (2) now reads: there is a highway region the subject occupies, an intersection lying on that highway, and the declared `int.left_turn` of the subject at that intersection.\n- The intention still decides which intersection is meant. No distance bound was added, because one would have narrowed the exception.\n- I recorded this as a disclosed reading on k10 (intention category).\n\n**The coder's second defect (emergency vehicles, k18, and road work, k14):**\n- **What I can't fix here:** this run's reading leaves every vehicle class unresolved as an authorized emergency vehicle. Any subject showing an emergency lamp therefore gets an unknown verdict. The reading isn't mine to change.\n- **What I changed:** the k18 \"on duty\" conduct is now a red or blue lamp, flashing or rotating, or a siren. Amber is the k14 work lamp, so a highway-maintenance vehicle with only its amber lamp on is now decided as not on emergency duty. Its exception can therefore be shown by a decided scenario.\n- **Trade-off:** this narrows the k18 exception. An authorized emergency vehicle showing only amber or white lamps is not excused, and the k18 narrowing says so.\n\n**Scenarios:**\n- The old `branch_4` (emergency vehicle, expected not applicable) can only ever come out unknown, so I removed it. With it gone, no scenario shows the k18 exception applying.\n- The new `branch_4` is the highway-maintenance vehicle with its amber lamp on (expected compliant).\n- `branch_6` is a declared left turn at an intersection on the subject's highway (compliant).\n- `branch_7` is the same scene with no left turn planned (violated).\n\n**Other changes:**\n- The catalogued assumption and intention ids are reused with no `meaning` field.\n- `param_proposals` is now empty: every parameter the record uses is already in the catalogue.\n\nThe coding session will need to add a highway region and the intersection's on-highway relation to the left-turn scenarios. If nothing in the library tests whether an exception can ever apply, k18 may still be flagged for that.",
